name w1-06-strike-escort-1
timeout 520

# CAMPAIGN W1, SORTIE 6 OF 10 - OFFENSIVE COUNTER-AIR: A STRIKE WITH ITS ESCORT, RUNG 6 OF THE LADDER.
# Spec, anchor and sources: doc/campaigns/w1-red-flag.md. Format: doc/missions/campaign.md.
# CONTROL: none. The degree of freedom this rung adds over rung 5 is the SECOND BLUE ROLE - a package
# with two jobs in one file instead of one - and Blue is the side with the ground task for the first time.
#
# THE ANCHOR: "offensive counter air" and "dynamic targeting" are two of the five mission types the 414th
# CTS fact sheet names [T1, Wayback capture 20240116184035]; the target array is the fact sheet's own list
# ("mock airfields, vehicle convoys, tanks, parked aircraft, bunkered defensive positions, missile
# sites"). The ARENA is w1-01's lane, `--elev const`, 0 m range floor. Every coordinate [SET].
#
# THE ONE TACTICAL QUESTION: does the escort stay tied to the strikers, or does it chase the picture and
# leave them naked?
#
# C12 AGAIN SUPERSEDES THE SPEC'S BLOCKER (campaign rule 7). The spec says *"there is no escort role -
# C12, C15"*. There is still no escort ROLE, and there does not need to be: doc/missions/verdict.md states
# it outright - *"escort is not a kind. It is `protect unit X` plus a station requirement"* - and the first
# half has been declarable since round C12. Each escort therefore declares `protect unit` on BOTH strikers,
# so "did the escort keep them alive" is a machine-read verdict rather than a reading of the telemetry.
# WHAT IS STILL MISSING IS THE SECOND HALF: no station requirement, no time-on-target, no deconfliction,
# no lead tasking (C15). The escort holds nothing; it flies its own vector and fights what it finds.
#
# THE TWO ENGAGEMENTS ARE SEPARATED IN TIME (O1's rule 6, and the run's whole record depends on it).
# `FBMissionRunner` ends the run at the FIRST flight-monitor K.O., and a mission-killed jet needs 50-120 s
# to reach the ground, so the strike has to be complete before anything falls. The geometry is built for
# it and the numbers are stated so the reader can check them: the strikers enter at -115.85, 25.7 km from
# their aim points, and reach them at 231 m/s in about 111 s; the escorts enter at -115.80 against an
# aggressor CAP at -116.58, i.e. 69.1 km apart closing at about 480 m/s, so the first Rtr shot cannot fall
# before about 105 s and the resulting ground contact not before about 170 s. Release BEFORE the first
# K.O., by design and by arithmetic.
#
# THE STRIKERS FLY RADAR-SILENT (`set fcr_mode off`) and carry Mk-84s only. That is not an EMCON
# experiment - rung 7 is - it is the same convention W3 and W4 use, and it is forced: the SMS steps
# stations in ascending order and a striker that also carried an AIM-120 on a low station would offer that
# round to the bomb pass and have the release refused for want of a lock (doc/duels.md D4).
#
# THE GROUND: three objects, the spec's own array. `nvcvy6` and `nvpk6` are the two aim points - a vehicle
# convoy and a row of parked aircraft, both `target_soft`, and a Mk-84's lethal radius against one is
# 100 m against a measured CCRP delivery error of ~22 m (doc/air-to-ground.md, doc/missions/weapons.md).
# `nvbnk6` is a bunkered defensive position and is NOT an aim point: the same Mk-84 needs 17.7 m against a
# `target_hard`, which is INSIDE the delivery error, so a hardened object is present as what it is on this
# range - a thing that survives being bombed - and the campaign says so rather than aiming at it.
#
# MEASURED (2026-07-30, campaign step 6 AND standalone - fingerprint 423844acb453ed54, identical):
# exit 3. THE ESCORT STAYS TIED FOR EXACTLY AS LONG AS THE STRIKE LASTS, AND THEN LEAVES.
#   the strike   both strikers released (t = 80.1 and 94.9 s, `ttrS` 0.586/0.555 against a 0.6 s lead),
#                `aimErrM` **13.07 m** and **18.87 m**, both aim points DESTROYED at t = 114.9 and
#                130.3 s. `aimAcrossM` 7.25 and 7.28 m - calm air
#   the escort   separation escort1 <-> striker1: 4.42 km at t = 0, **0.49 km at the release**, 4.47 km at
#                t = 100, 7.15 km at t = 200 - and then **45.40 km at t = 300, a peak of 60.30 km at
#                t = 383.5 s** and 57.42 km at the end. IT HELD THROUGH THE STRIKE AND ABANDONED THE
#                RECOVERY, which is doc/formation.md F1's rejoin gap arriving at package scale
#   the verdict  `protect unit rf6str1` **met** and `protect unit rf6str2` **met** on both escorts;
#                `kill team hostile` unmet. So the machine-read escort verdict is a PASS
#   the air fight one AIM-120 at **4.680 m** on `rf6agr2` (degraded, no kill) and one R-27R at
#                **12.001 m** on `rf6esc2` - INSIDE the 13.8 m fuze and not a kill, which is O2's rule
#                arriving in a seventh theatre. Nobody died
#   the time order the last release is t = 94.9 s and the first air-to-air arrival t = 106.7 s: the strike
#                was complete 11.8 s before anything could have ended the run. O1's rule 6 held by
#                arithmetic rather than by luck
#   the bunker   `nvbnk6` INTACT and never aimed at, as the header says
# SO THE ANSWER IS: TIED WHERE IT MATTERS, GONE AFTERWARDS. There is no station requirement to hold it
# (C15), and the 60.3 km says what a `protect` objective without one buys.
#
# WHAT TO READ: `pilot ATTACK_RELEASE` and `stores DELIVERY aimErrM`/`aimAcrossM` per striker (did the
# strike work), `mission OBJECTIVE unit=rf6esc* kind="protect unit rf6str*"` (did the escort do its job),
# the separation in TIME between the last `stores IMPACT` and the first `damage KILL`, and `flt_*` on the
# escort pair.
#
# READING RULE: exit 3 = TIMEOUT is the expected shape, because the escorts' `kill team hostile` needs
# both aggressors down. The verdict is the TRIPLE (aim points destroyed, escorts' protect state, the time
# order of release against the first kill). exit 1 means a striker was lost and the escorts FAILed with
# it - which is an answer to this file's question and not a defect. exit 2 would be a defect.

unit rf6str1
  team friendly
  flight str6 1
  module f16
  spawn 37.30000 -115.85000 5000 270.0 450
  set gear up
  set fuel_pct 80
  set fcr_mode off                            # a striker does not radiate
  set attack_mode ccrp
  set rwr on
  set datalink on
  set store 3 mk84
  set store 7 mk84
  set cmds_mode auto
  set cmds_program 1
  set cmds_chaff 60
  set cmds_flare 60
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set task attack
  wp 37.30000 -116.14000 5000 450             # aim point: the vehicle convoy
  wp 37.34000 -115.80000 5200 450             # egress east, back toward Nellis
  objective kill unit nvcvy6
  objective survive

unit rf6str2
  team friendly
  flight str6 2
  module f16
  spawn 37.28198 -115.85000 5150 270.0 450
  set gear up
  set fuel_pct 80
  set fcr_mode off
  set attack_mode ccrp
  set rwr on
  set datalink on
  set store 3 mk84
  set store 7 mk84
  set cmds_mode auto
  set cmds_program 1
  set cmds_chaff 60
  set cmds_flare 60
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set task attack
  wp 37.28198 -116.18000 5150 450             # aim point: the parked-aircraft row
  wp 37.24000 -115.80000 5350 450
  objective kill unit nvpk6
  objective survive

unit rf6esc1
  team friendly
  flight esc6 1
  module f16
  spawn 37.30000 -115.80000 6500 270.0 480
  set gear up
  set fuel_pct 80
  set datalink on
  set fcr_mode crm
  set fcr_range_nm 40
  set rwr on
  set store 1 aim120
  set store 2 aim120
  set store 3 aim120
  set store 4 aim120
  set store 6 aim9
  set store 7 aim9
  set cmds_mode auto
  set cmds_program 1
  set cmds_chaff 60
  set cmds_flare 60
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set task intercept
  wp 37.30000 -116.58000 6500 480
  objective kill team hostile
  objective protect unit rf6str1
  objective protect unit rf6str2
  objective survive

unit rf6esc2
  team friendly
  flight esc6 2
  module f16
  spawn 37.31802 -115.80000 6650 270.0 480
  set gear up
  set fuel_pct 80
  set datalink on
  set fcr_mode crm
  set fcr_range_nm 40
  set rwr on
  set store 1 aim120
  set store 2 aim120
  set store 3 aim120
  set store 4 aim120
  set store 6 aim9
  set store 7 aim9
  set cmds_mode auto
  set cmds_program 1
  set cmds_chaff 60
  set cmds_flare 60
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set task intercept
  wp 37.31802 -116.58000 6650 480
  objective kill team hostile
  objective protect unit rf6str1
  objective protect unit rf6str2
  objective survive

unit rf6agr1
  team hostile
  flight agr6 1
  module mig29
  spawn 37.30000 -116.58000 6000 90.0 450
  set gear up
  set fuel_pct 70
  set n019_mode rad
  set n019_range_nm 27
  set n019_emission illum
  set kols_mode ir
  set rwr on
  set brief_sort left
  set store 3 r27r
  set store 4 r27r
  set store 5 r73
  set store 6 r73
  set store 1 r73
  set store 2 r73
  set cmds_mode man
  set cmds_program 1
  set cmds_chaff 30
  set cmds_flare 30
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set task intercept
  wp 37.30000 -115.60000 6000 450
